<title>USA: MTS Systems gets $1.5 mln EPA contract.</title>
<headline>MTS Systems gets $1.5 mln EPA contract.</headline>
<dateline>EDEN PRAIRIE, Minn. 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>MTS Systems Corp said Wednesday the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency awarded a $1.5 million contract to a subsidiary of MTS for two engine test cells.</p>
<p>The test cells will be used in developing new engine technology and reducing engine emissions.</p>
<p>Delivery of the systems is planned for spring 1997.</p>
<p>MTS manufactures computer-based testing and simulation systems.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
